This is Spork's Gehennom, not vanilla's.  It's cavern, not maze -- this
means that it's much easier to directly traverse.  The threat comes from
the potential to be surrounded by monsters, something that couldn't
happen in vanilla's mazes.

Also, the mysterious force is removed in Spork; it simply added nothing
but annoyance to the game.  The design intent appears to have been "it
should be difficult to get out of Gehennom"; i've been switching the
'difficult' part over from "annoying" to "fight your way back out".

> It's interesting to now see a thread where the player shall be slowed
> down in Gehennom; 

That isn't what is being suggested or discussed here at all.  Right now,
Spork has no force and Gehennom is cavernous, but Rodney intervenes more
often, monsters generate at an extremely high rate, and you can no
longer teleport while carrying the Amulet.  Much less boring.

The proposal at hand is whether providing some sort of limited teleportation 
while carrying the Amulet is a good idea, or whether it renders Gehennom 
_too_ easy.  So far, most of what I've seen falls onto the side of 'too 
easy', including my own suggestion; so I'm still looking to see if there 
are ways to limit the effectiveness while still allowing the ability.

